  "id": "gzip.crc-trailer.identity-mismatch",
  "divergence": "D1",
  "reason": "D1: the port reads the gzip container of an archive strictly. CPython reads it lazily, in 8 KiB steps and only as far as the tar listing and the one manifest need, never checks the CRC-32 and length trailer it does not reach, and lets a truncated stream escape as EOFError or zlib.error, which archive.py:138 does not catch. The port decompresses and checks the whole container first and refuses any damage as \"unreadable archive or manifest\". On a damaged container the port answers before it looks at the tar stream, so a refusal the oracle would have given for the content is replaced: here the manifest names another package and the CRC-32 trailer is wrong. The oracle refuses with E_ARCHIVE_IDENTITY; the port refuses with E_ADAPTER_INPUT. The public code changes.",
